Q: Simplest way to merge ES6 Maps/Sets? A: <p>While <code>Set</code>s now have a <code>union</code> method, there is no such equivalent for <code>Map</code>s. Fortunately, as of March 2025, all major browsers support <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Iterator#iterator_helper_methods" rel="nofollow noreferrer">iterator helpers</a>. Since <code>Map</code>s are iterable and are constructed from iterables, you can concatenate iterators to merge two <code>Map</code>s without constructing an intermediate array:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const a = new Map([['a', 1], ['b', 2]])
const b = new Map([['c', 3], ['a', 4]])

new Map([a, b].values().flatMap(map =&gt; map))
// -&gt; Map(3) {'a' =&gt; 4, 'b' =&gt; 2, 'c' =&gt; 3}
</code></pre>
<p>As of March 2026, only Firefox supports a convenience method <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Iterator/concat" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Iterator.concat</code></a>, which simplifies this a bit more:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>new Map(Iterator.concat(a, b))
// -&gt; Map(3) {'a' =&gt; 4, 'b' =&gt; 2, 'c' =&gt; 3}
</code></pre>

Q: Aligning buttons inside div and span between buttons A: <p>You can do this. You need to replace <strong>inside</strong> word by <strong>between</strong> word. The span in your case is not inside the buttons.</p>

<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>button{
  background-color:darkblue;
  color:white;
  padding:5px 10px;
  border:none;
  font-size:20px;
}

#stripe &gt;*{
  vertical-align:top;/*or bottom, middle....*/
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div id="stripe"&gt;
  &lt;button id="new"&gt;New Colors&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;span id="message"&gt;Some message&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;button id="easy"&gt;Easy&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;button id="hard"&gt;Hard&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

